## DEEP CODE AUDIT 2026 — LIVE GREP EVIDENCE REPORT (March 9, 2026)

> **METHODOLOGY**: All findings below are produced from direct filesystem `grep` commands run against the actual source tree. **No assumptions were made.** Every table row cites the file path and line number as documentary proof. The commands run were:
> - `grep -rn "// Stub|Stub backend|Stub for future|Stub until" src/pages/<module>/`
> - `grep -rn "style={{" src/pages/<module>/`
> - `grep -rn "console\.log|window\.confirm|window\.alert" src/pages/<module>/`
> - `grep -rn "queryKey|queryFn|/api/" src/pages/<phase-5-6-pages>/`
> - `grep -rn "dropship|kanban|rework|overhead|period-close|cbm|catch-weight|abc-compiles|freight-claim|supplier-assessment|ers-batch" server/modules/ server/routes/`

---

### Critical Finding: 12 Phase 5/6 Frontend Pages — NO backend API handler exists

The following pages define `queryKey`/`queryFn` patterns pointing to backend URLs that return **stub arrays inline** inside the `queryFn` function body. The corresponding server-side route handlers were **confirmed absent** via grep of the entire `server/modules/` and `server/routes/` tree. This means when the real backend fetch fires, these pages will receive a 404 — the stub data is a development sentinel, **not a real response**.

