### Tertiary Finding: UI Primitives in Old Core SCM Pages

Older SCM pages (pre-standardization) contain raw HTML input elements and placeholder-only forms without Zod validation or proper react-hook-form bindings:

| File | Issue |
|---|---|
| `src/pages/PurchaseOrders.tsx` | Lines 93–95: `<Input placeholder="Vendor ID" />` — bare uncontrolled inputs, no RHF binding |
| `src/pages/GoodsReceipt.tsx` | Line 87: `<Input placeholder="Inspection Notes..." />` — uncontrolled, disconnected from state |
| `src/pages/GoodsReceiptPutaway.tsx` | Lines 80–82: Manual `setNewReceipt` state, not using `react-hook-form` + Zod |
| `src/pages/ProcurementSourcing.tsx` | Lines 84–87: Same raw state mutation pattern without form validation |

